From 704c094b319effaccc2e00e33f998830b10c9abe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 09:49:57 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] www: header button group, kit pages on a phone, DNS Director
 names, pop-up panels centred in the shell

- Header (owner, iPhone 17 portrait): ? / Reboot / Logout are one group (.acts, data-rfit-keep)
  on the dashboard and in the shell. It fits beside the logo or wraps whole, and fit.js never
  squeezes it for another element's overflow - on the dashboard the clipping ancestor is the page
  body, so a live tile spilling past a phone screen shrank the two buttons and they sprang back on
  the next pass. Under 430 px the group takes its own row.
- Phones: rp.css ends with a 680 px block (settings rows in one column, data tables pan in their
  own box, tighter padding) and fit.js leaves the headers of a panning table whole; all 32 kit
  pages are screen width at 402, 375 and 320 px in the mock. The dashboard's phone strip matches
  the shell's (language row and group headings hidden, About mark only, logo capped at 28 px).
- DNS Director: per-device rules show the device name beside the MAC (the user's names, then the
  rule's own name; set as text).
- Pop-up panels (owner: the AiMesh client card opened near the top of the page): form.js
  adjust_panel_block_top() placed a panel at the framed page's scrollTop, which is always 0 inside
  reaper_shell. In the shell it now centres the panel in the slice of the page the user can see,
  read through the shell's synchronous reaperAnchorNow() (reaper_shell.asp); the stock path
  outside the shell is unchanged.
Other hunk: Main_ReaperDash.asp's WPS and MLO rows open the kit pages of the earlier commit.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
